<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine pension funds yield 20.42 pct.</title>
<headline>Argentine pension funds yield 20.42 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's private pension funds achieved an average return of 20.42 percent on their investments in the year to September, the Superintendencia de AFJPs, the body that monitors the funds, said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The maximum return attained was 26.54 percent while the lowest return was 14.29 percent, said the Superintendencia.</p>
<p>The annualized return since the private pension funds were first established in the middle of 1994 was 16.69 percent.</p>
<p>-- Walter Bianchi, Buenos Aires Newsroom, +54 1 318-0633</p>
</text>
